# WNBA Verification Agent

The Verification Agent is a deterministic in-app pipeline (not an LLM). It
pulls official traditional box scores from `stats.wnba.com` (the API behind
wnba.com), diffs them against our final canonical rows, and opens review-queue
findings. It never overwrites `wnba_*` box-score tables.

Orchestrator: `app/Services/WNBA/Agents/VerificationService.php`, queued via
`app/Jobs/RunVerificationAgent.php`. Triggered by the nightly chain after the
Entity Agent, `app:wnba-agent verification`, or
`POST /api/wnba/data/agent-run` with `agent=verification`. Weekly full-season
sweep: Mondays 04:00 (`--mode=season`).

## Non-negotiable rules

1. **Oracle is verify-only.** Do not add `wnba_stats` to
   `config('wnba.agents.source_priority')` or write box scores from this agent.
2. **Raw payloads first.** Store schedule and box responses via
   `RawPayloadStore` with `source_id = wnba_stats` (skipped on `--dry-run`).
3. **No name-only player matches.** Join games by date + home/away
   abbreviations (`TeamCatalog`). Join players by `wnba_stats_player_id`, or
   a unique counting-stat fingerprint when exactly one unmapped candidate
   exists. Ambiguous joins → `oracle_player_unmapped` / `oracle_game_unmapped`.
4. **Findings only.** Mismatches go to `wnba_data_conflicts` with
   `requires_review = true` and candidates
   `[{source_id: canonical, value}, {source_id: wnba_stats, value}]`. Identical
   open findings are not duplicated.
5. **Never invent values.** Missing oracle data stays a finding or a skip —
   never a fabricated fill for our tables.
6. **Finals only.** Skip in-progress / scheduled games. Default lookback is
   `WNBA_VERIFY_LOOKBACK_DAYS` (3); `--mode=season` verifies the whole season.

## Identity columns

- `wnba_games.wnba_stats_game_id`
- `wnba_players.wnba_stats_player_id`
- `wnba_teams.wnba_stats_team_id`

Persist mappings when a join is deterministic and collision-free. Do not clear
existing mappings from this agent.

## Finding shapes

| entity_type | entity_key | field |
|---|---|---|
| `player_game_stat` | `{game.game_id}\|{athlete_id}` | stat column / `minutes` / `missing_from_oracle` |
| `team_game_stat` | `{game.game_id}\|{team_id}` | `team_score` or counting stat |
| `game` | `game_id` | `oracle_game_unmapped` / `oracle_fetch_failed` |
| `player` | oracle person id | `oracle_player_unmapped` |

## Chain position

Nightly: **data → entity → verification → analytics**. Analytics must not
depend on verification success for writes in v1; verification findings are
informational review-queue items.

## Run contract

`AgentRunReporter` agent name `verification`. Modes: `audit` (lookback),
`season` (full season). Counters: `findings_games_checked`,
`findings_games_unmapped`, `findings_stat_mismatches`,
`findings_players_unmapped`, `findings_players_missing`, `findings_ids_linked`,
`review_queue_added`. Status follows the shared reporter rules
(`success` / `partial` / `failed`).
